    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [x] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version of the `main` branch\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.git\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.11.x\n\n### Description\n\nWhen using `mini.git` on FreeBSD, under certain conditions the following error is produced when running a `git` command in a terminal (e.g. `git status`):\n\n```\nError executing callback:\nvim/shared.lua:823: s: expected string, got nil\nstack traceback:\n        [C]: in function 'error'\n        vim/shared.lua:1045: in function 'validate'\n        vim/shared.lua:823: in function 'endswith'\n        ...are/nvim/site/pack/deps/start/mini.nvim/lua/mini/git.lua:1308: in function <...are/nvim/site/pack/deps/start/mini.nvim/lua/mini/git.lua:1306>\n```\n\nThis corresponds to the following code:\n\nhttps://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/2809a06d24fe528c572c7ceca4f0a82fecb02ea8/lua/mini/git.lua#L1308\n\nThe error only happens sporadically, but when it happens it keeps happening until I restart Neovim. Sadly I do not yet have a way to reproduce this on its own, as it seems to happen quite randomly. However, the uv documentation about [`uv_fs_event_cb`](https://docs.libuv.org/en/v1.x/fs_event.html#c.uv_fs_event_cb) says the following:\n\n> If the handle was started with a directory the filename parameter will be a relative path to a file contained in the directory, **or NULL if the file name cannot be determined.**\n\nThis bit was added in https://github.com/libuv/libuv/pull/4177 in relation to https://github.com/libuv/libuv/issues/4160. That however seems Windows specific, so I suspect it may not be directly related.\n\nI bit of digging through the uv code reveals the following cases where `NULL` is (potentially) passed to `filename`, translating to `nil` in Lua:\n\n- https://github.com/libuv/libuv/blob/91ae02a63d25caccddd835fb201195fefe9d113b/src/unix/fsevents.c#L178\n- https://github.com/libuv/libuv/blob/91ae02a63d25caccddd835fb201195fefe9d113b/src/unix/fsevents.c#L189\n\nThat first link in particular seems to suggest that in the event of an error, uv still calls the callback but passes an error flag and `NULL` for the file name, though it's not clear under what circumstances that would occur.\n\nFor now I've modified the code to log some extra data when the file name is nil/NULL to see what's going on.\n\n### Reproduction\n\n1. Create separate 'nvim-repro' config directory:\n    - '~/.config/nvim-repro/' on Unix\n    - '~/AppData/Local/nvim-repro/' on Windows\n\n2. Inside 'nvim-repro' directory create a file named 'init.lua'.\n   Populate it with the following content:\n\n    ```lua\n    -- Clone latest 'mini.nvim' (requires Git CLI installed)\n    vim.cmd('echo \"Installing `mini.nvim`\" | redraw')\n    local mini_path = vim.fn.stdpath('data') .. '/site/pack/deps/start/mini.nvim'\n    local clone_cmd = { 'git', 'clone', '--depth=1', 'https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim', mini_path }\n    vim.fn.system(clone_cmd)\n    vim.cmd('echo \"`mini.nvim` is installed\" | redraw')\n\n    -- Make sure 'mini.nvim' is available\n    vim.cmd('packadd mini.nvim')\n    require('mini.deps').setup()\n\n    -- Add extra setup steps needed to reproduce the behavior\n    -- Use `MiniDeps.add('user/repo')` to install another plugin from GitHub\n    ```\n\n3. Run `NVIM_APPNAME=nvim-repro nvim` (i.e. execute `nvim` with `NVIM_APPNAME` environment variable set to \"nvim-repro\").\n   Wait for all dependencies to install.\n\n4. Replace this with description of interactive reproduction steps along with the behavior you observe.\n   Feel free to include images/videos/etc, this helps a lot.\n\n<details><summary>What to do after reporting an issue</summary>\n\nAfter reporting the issue, it is safe (and even recommended for cleaner possible future bug reports) to remove 'nvim-repro' config from the system:\n- Delete config directory ('~/.config/nvim-repro' on Unix).\n- Delete data directory ('~/.local/share/nvim-repro' on Unix).\n- Delete state directory ('~/.local/state/nvim-repro' on Unix).\n\n</details>\n",
