            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "Speaking of the devil: as I was about to submit this issue it happened again, this time with the logging data. For that data I modified `git.lua` as follows:\n\n```diff\ndiff --git a/lua/mini/git.lua b/lua/mini/git.lua\nindex 1ba36b42..732cd8ed 100644\n--- a/lua/mini/git.lua\n+++ b/lua/mini/git.lua\n@@ -1303,7 +1303,11 @@ H.setup_repo_watch = function(buf_id, repo)\n     local fs_event, timer = vim.loop.new_fs_event(), vim.loop.new_timer()\n\n     local on_change = vim.schedule_wrap(function() H.on_repo_change(repo) end)\n-    local watch = function(_, filename, _)\n+    local watch = function(_, filename, events, status)\n+      if not filename then\n+        print('filename is nil: ' .. vim.inspect({ events, status }))\n+      end\n+\n       -- Ignore temporary changes\n       if vim.endswith(filename, 'lock') then return end\n```\n\nThe output of `:messages` is now as follows:\n\n```\nfilename is nil: { {\n    rename = true\n  } }\nError executing callback:\nvim/shared.lua:823: s: expected string, got nil\nstack traceback:\n        [C]: in function 'error'\n        vim/shared.lua:1045: in function 'validate'\n        vim/shared.lua:823: in function 'endswith'\n        ...are/nvim/site/pack/deps/start/mini.nvim/lua/mini/git.lua:1312: in function <...are/nvim/site/pack/deps/start/mini.nvim/lua/mini/git.lua:1306>\nfilename is nil: { {\n    rename = true\n  } }\nError executing callback:\nvim/shared.lua:823: s: expected string, got nil\nstack traceback:\n        [C]: in function 'error'\n        vim/shared.lua:1045: in function 'validate'\n        vim/shared.lua:823: in function 'endswith'\n        ...are/nvim/site/pack/deps/start/mini.nvim/lua/mini/git.lua:1312: in function <...are/nvim/site/pack/deps/start/mini.nvim/lua/mini/git.lua:1306>\n```",
