            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue and very thorough investigation (expected no less from you :) )!\n\n> I'm still very new to FreeBSD so I can't really judge as to what's going on here, but given FreeBSD's small userbase (and thus getting less attention/care from projects) it may very well be a bug in either the luv bindings or uv itself.\n\nAfter reading this I do agree that this looks like an upstream issue. And it looks like a good idea to report somewhere upstream also.\n\nHowever, the 'mini.git' change to account for this is rather trivial and given the sever consequences (renders whole Neovim unusable) seems okay to add. Just to be sure, does applying the following patch fix the issue?\n\n```diff\ndiff --git a/lua/mini/git.lua b/lua/mini/git.lua\nindex 1ba36b42..c98183d1 100644\n--- a/lua/mini/git.lua\n+++ b/lua/mini/git.lua\n@@ -1305,7 +1305,7 @@ H.setup_repo_watch = function(buf_id, repo)\n     local on_change = vim.schedule_wrap(function() H.on_repo_change(repo) end)\n     local watch = function(_, filename, _)\n       -- Ignore temporary changes\n-      if vim.endswith(filename, 'lock') then return end\n+      if vim.endswith(filename or '', 'lock') then return end\n \n       -- Debounce to not overload during incremental staging (like in script)\n       timer:stop()\n```",
